        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(browser): prove post-action target continuity before adopting a tab",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nAfter a browser navigation or action invalidates the selected raw target, route code retried tab lists and adopted replacements via heuristics: any sole remaining tab, a uniquely new post-action tab, or a uniquely URL-matching tab. None of those prove the acted-on page identity, so `/act` could return an unrelated tab's `targetId` and silently redirect the caller's next mutating action onto the wrong page.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nClawSweeper's recommended path: make each backend return its operation-owned target outcome; remove route-level list inference entirely. Playwright navigate/act now read the acted-on page's raw target id via `Target.getTargetInfo` after the operation and return it on the result. Routes apply `resolveOperationTargetOutcome`: backend-reported id when present, otherwise the acted-on id (stale/closed) so callers require a fresh selection.\n\nRemoved heuristics:\n- adopting a uniquely new post-action tab\n- adopting a uniquely URL-matching tab (renderer swap inferred from lists)\n\nChrome MCP existing-session and extension-relay stable tab identity vs volatile attachment identity remain deferred to their backend owners; those paths keep the acted-on id until wired.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- **Playwright navigate/act:** response `targetId` is the backend-owned identity of the page that executed the operation. If the page closes, the acted-on id is returned (stale) and callers must re-select.\n- **No wrong-tab routing:** unrelated tabs left open are never adopted from tab lists, URL cardinality, or sole-tab fallback.\n- **Continuity preserved:** renderer swaps and action-triggered replacements still work when Playwright reports the new raw target id (#25323 / #25326 / #46137).\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Live browser proof (real Chrome, backend page identity)\n\nHarness: `extensions/browser/scripts/proof-103785-target-continuity.test-harness.mts`\n\nRun:\n\n```\npnpm exec tsx extensions/browser/scripts/proof-103785-target-continuity.test-harness.mts\n```\n\nRedacted output:\n\n```\n=== Live-browser proof for #103785 (backend-owned page identity) ===\n\nScenario A: action closes acted-on tab A; unrelated tab B survives\n  kept acted-on identity A: true\n  adopted unrelated survivor B: false\n  PASS: unrelated survivor B was NOT adopted.\n\nScenario B: renderer swap (page reattaches under new raw target at navigated url)\n  adopted backend-reported reattached target: true\n  PASS: renderer-swap continuity preserved.\n\n=== ALL SCENARIOS PASSED ===\n```\n\n### Source and test changes\n\n- `resolveOperationTargetOutcome` replaces list-inference resolver; no tab-list adoption.\n- `readPageTargetId` exported from Playwright session; `navigateViaPlaywright` and `executeActViaPlaywright` return `targetId`.\n- `/navigate` and Playwright `/act` paths wire backend outcomes; MCP/relay deferred.\n- Tests updated; contract test for #46137 mocks backend `targetId` on act result.\n\nAutomated tests:\n\n```\npnpm test:extension browser -- extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/agent.snapshot.test.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/server.agent-contract-core.test.ts\n# Test Files 2 passed (2) | Tests 30 passed (30)\n```\n\nExtension package boundary typecheck: `extension package boundary check passed`.\n\nCloses #103785\n",
        "branch": "fix/browser-post-action-target-continuity-103785",
